--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/eglantine-patches/1032-up-mesh-before-pass.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,487 @@
+From: EglantinePS5
+Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_MESH_BEFORE_PASS (off unless set): a task/mesh draw run as compute records its compute passes before the open render pass instead of ending the pass and beginning it again
+
+Idea and upstream patch: ronaldpena007-ops, zortos293/Lichii issue #1431 ("Mesh emulation cuts the
+render pass ~70 times a frame on AMD", EDEN_NX2_MESH_BEFORE_PASS). Ported by hand to our own mesh-as-
+compute path (lone mesh draws, the T47 line; GraphicsPipeline::RecordMeshComputePasses), which differs
+from upstream's: one shared scratch region (MeshComputeScratch) every draw used from offset 0, push
+constants that carry the region's address to the readback vertex shader, no per-draw descriptor cell.
+
+Why: RecordMeshComputePasses called RequestOutsideRenderPassOperationContext for every mesh draw:
+the open pass ended, the compute passes ran, the pass began again (LOAD) for the readback draw.
+Upstream counted ~70 such cuts a frame in the field; their patch moved 96 % of them before the pass
+(GPU busy went down on an RDNA 3.5 iGPU, fps unchanged there because the CPU split was the limit).
+
+What (EDEN_UP_MESH_BEFORE_PASS=1, or =2):
+- Scheduler::BeginRenderPassImpl records a prelude runner just before the pass's begin. While the
+  begin's chunk has not gone to the worker (DispatchWork resets it; so does the pass's end), a mesh
+  draw of that pass appends its compute passes to the prelude (Scheduler::ReserveBeforePass +
+  RecordBeforePass) instead of cutting the pass.
+- Each such draw gets its own place in the scratch region (256-byte aligned, after the prelude's
+  earlier draws and after a draw whose readback is still to come: NoteMeshScratchWritten /
+  NoteMeshScratchRead). Its FillBuffer, indirect dispatch, push constants and readback DrawIndirect
+  use that offset. A draw that does not fit cuts the pass as before.
+- The readback draw pushes the draw's MeshComputeLayout again (the region's address): another draw's
+  passes may have run since its own. Only with the switch.
+- Refused (the pass is cut as before) when: the draw writes storage, samples a render target of its
+  pass, or feeds transform feedback; a draw of the pass wrote storage; a batched upload waits; the
+  pass's begin went to the worker; the rescaling state at the begin differs (the passes push the down
+  factor that the pass's earlier draws read); the region is full. The passes bind the draw's
+  descriptor buffer chunk: they bind the chunk the pass began with again after them.
+- =1 also holds the rasterizer's periodic DispatchWork (every 32 draws) while a prelude is open, so
+  the window lasts until the chunk is full (as upstream; we hold no extra chunks). =2: no hold.
+Not ported from upstream: the held-chunk queue (up to 32 full chunks kept from the worker) and the
+deferred-clear case (a pending clear begun as the draw's pass to take the prelude).
+
+Count line (powers of two of events): "EDEN_UP_MESH_BEFORE_PASS: N mesh draws ran before their pass,
+M did not (begin sent, no pass, draw writes storage or samples a target, pass wrote storage, other
+target, uploads, rescaling, no room)", and one boot line when on.
+
+Unset (the default): the passes are recorded exactly as before (offset 0, pass cut), no prelude, no
+extra push, the periodic dispatch as before: as T181. Files: vk_scheduler.{h,cpp},
+vk_graphics_pipeline.{h,cpp}, vk_rasterizer.cpp: none is a translation id input; the new name is not
+in TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.
