diff --git a/tools/eglantine-patches/1040-up-jit-x64-opt-lichii1531.patch b/tools/eglantine-patches/1040-up-jit-x64-opt-lichii1531.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..741bcfa28b26b0a3a12b7a291faaddf0c31f953e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/eglantine-patches/1040-up-jit-x64-opt-lichii1531.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,516 @@
+From: EglantinePS5
+Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_JIT_X64_OPT=1, four of Lichii PR #1531's dynarmic x64 code generation options (off by default)
+
+Ported from zortos293/Lichii aab5393019 (PR #1531, "dynarmic: x86-64 code generation from #831"),
+author Zortos, co-authors Julius Bairaktaris and the PR's own sources: #717 by
+stephenjayakar and #641. Lichii sets these options for every CPU accuracy but Paranoid; here they
+are behind one switch read once at JIT creation (ArmDynarmic64::MakeJit).
+
+EDEN_UP_JIT_X64_OPT=1 sets in A64 UserConfig (all default false, so unset the emitted code is T181's):
+- scratch_copy_to_free_reg: when an instruction overwrites an operand that is still needed, the
+  register allocator writes into a copy in a free register (SelectARegister picked an empty one)
+  instead of evicting the original (RegAlloc::UseScratchImpl).
+- elide_redundant_zext: SetW and ZeroExtendWordToLong skip `mov r32, r32` for a value in a GPR
+  that a 32-bit instruction produced (A64GetW, A64ReadMemory32, LeastSignificantWord, Add32, Sub32,
+  ConditionalSelect32). With upstream's later fix: only for a value in a register (a spill slot holds
+  just 32 bits); here SetW asks for a register too. The front's XMM case of ZeroExtendWordToLong
+  (scalar-memory.cmake) still comes first.
+- omit_block_frame: A64 blocks no longer save %rbp, point it at the StackLayout and restore it.
+- reuse_host_flags (no cycle counting only): Add/Sub with a GetNZCVFromOp record where their host
+  flags end; an A64SetNZCV of that value right after keeps them marked live (also across the
+  movs of SetW/SetX and the %rbp restore), and EmitCond (If terminals: B.cond) and CSEL then use
+  the host flags (cmc for HI/LS, as sahf+cmc) instead of reloading NZCV from the JIT state. NZCV is
+  still stored. Upstream's CheckBit-in-ZF part is left out: the front's EDEN_JIT_CHECKBIT_FLAGS
+  (fast_paths.cmake) owns those two functions by exact text.
+
+Lines: "EDEN_UP_JIT_X64_OPT core=<n> scratch_copy=1 zext=1 no_frame=1 flags=<0|1>" per JIT, and
+"EDEN_UP_JIT_X64_OPT blocks=<n> frame_omitted=1 scratch_copies=<n> zext_elided=<n> flags_reused=<n>"
+at the 16th compiled block and every power of two (process-wide counts).
+
+Left out of #1531 (not in this patch): host_call_return, halt_check_on_back_edges, compact_block_exits
+and rsb_size (the front replaces the A64 link terminals, PushRSB, the JIT state's RSB and Jit::Impl
+with its shared-JIT versions: shared-jit.cmake, jit_links.inc, jit_push_rsb.inc, jit_impl.inc);
+fast_dispatch_table_bits/set_associative (the table is the front's per-core table, sized by
+EDEN_JIT_DISPATCH_BITS); far_code (EDEN_UP_JIT_COLD_CHUNKS does this here, and the code space is a
+W^X alias); fold_address_offsets (needs a 64-bit fastmem arena, the console has none); spill_to_free_gpr
+(EDEN_JIT_FREE_MOVES, ProsperoEden PR 189, does it); the PushRSB dispatch fix (the front already
+makes it); the tests.
+
+Interaction: with EDEN_JIT_CHECKBIT_FLAGS=1 the CheckBit fusion needs the %rbp restore's bytes, so
+under EDEN_UP_JIT_X64_OPT=1 it no longer fuses (it falls back to the compare: correct, as before
+the fusion).
+
+Not in the kept-store stamp: dynarmic and src/core/arm only. KEEPS THE STORE.
+
+T184 merge: rebased onto 1030 (EDEN_UP_JIT_REGALLOC_BITS). Context lines only: the added and
+removed lines are the same as the T184f original (c1da635). The fix both switches need together
+is in 1041.
